.TH GIT-@-CHANGELOG 1 "August 2025" "GitAT v1.1.0" "Git Workflow Management Tool"
.SH NAME
git-@-changelog \- Generate and manage changelogs based on conventional commits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git @ changelog
[\fICOMMAND\fR] [\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
The \fBchangelog\fR command generates and manages changelogs based on conventional commits. It automatically categorizes commits into appropriate sections based on their commit types.
.PP
The command follows the Keep a Changelog format (https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/) and integrates with conventional commit types for automatic categorization.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B generate, gen
Generate a new changelog (default action)
.TP
.B update
Update existing changelog
.TP
.B preview
Show a preview without saving
.TP
.B release <version>
Generate a release entry for specific version
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show help message
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
No additional options beyond the commands listed above.
.SH CONVENTIONAL COMMIT CATEGORIES
.PP
Commits are automatically categorized based on conventional commit types:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfeat\fR: Features
.IP \(bu 2
\fBfix\fR: Bug Fixes
.IP \(bu 2
\fBdocs\fR: Documentation
.IP \(bu 2
\fBrefactor\fR: Code Refactoring
.IP \(bu 2
\fBperf\fR: Performance Improvements
.IP \(bu 2
\fBtest\fR: Tests
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbuild\fR: Build System
.IP \(bu 2
\fBci\fR: Continuous Integration
.IP \(bu 2
\fBchore\fR: Chores
.IP \(bu 2
\fBstyle\fR: Code Style
.IP \(bu 2
All other commits: Other Changes
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Generate changelog:
.RS
.nf
git @ changelog
.fi
.RE
.PP
Update existing changelog:
.RS
.nf
git @ changelog update
.fi
.RE
.PP
Preview changelog:
.RS
.nf
git @ changelog preview
.fi
.RE
.PP
Generate release entry:
.RS
.nf
git @ changelog release v1.2.0
.fi
.RE
.SH FEATURES
.PP
The changelog command includes several features:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Automatic commit categorization based on conventional commit types
.IP \(bu 2
Release management with properly formatted release entries
.IP \(bu 2
File integration with CHANGELOG.md
.IP \(bu 2
Interactive prompts for confirmation before saving
.IP \(bu 2
Flexible output modes (preview, generate, update)
.RE
.SH FILE FORMAT
.PP
Generated changelogs follow the Keep a Changelog format:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
Header with project information
.IP \(bu 2
[Unreleased] section for upcoming changes
.IP \(bu 2
Categorized sections for different commit types
.IP \(bu 2
Properly formatted release entries with dates
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
.BR git-@ (1),
.BR git-@-rebase (1),
.BR git-@-commitizen (1)